      "problem": "Find $5det(A)+2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 1.5 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 1.5 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- For the matrix $B,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 3-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+2det(B)=5\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 3=6.$",
